<ArticleLayout slug="digital-humans-in-china" ctaLabel="Scope a digital human" faq={faq}>
  <p class="standfirst">Published Chinese prices for a brand digital human run from a few hundred RMB to 300,000 RMB and up, because they price different products. Whether any of them can go on air is decided by the deep synthesis provisions, the AI labeling measures and the livestream marketing measures.</p>

  <h2>How much does a digital human cost in China?</h2>

  <p>Chinese rate cards price a self-serve likeness clone at a few hundred to low thousands of RMB, a custom 2D presenter captured from a real person at 8,000 to 30,000 RMB, and a photoreal 3D character at 20,000 to 100,000 RMB on one 2026 table and 80,000 to 300,000 RMB and up on another. hubStudio prints no rate here.</p>

  <p>Those figures are not a spread around one price. They belong to different products, and every card below was published by someone who sells the thing it prices. The sections on consent and rules describe production practice drawn from the published text of each instrument. They are not legal advice.</p>

